Ê xalo tu... te berda? Bes e.
 
So uncle, you... you divorced? Enough.

162
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:44,000
Bes e... got wekî we te de de qaçaxî, qaçaxçîtiyê bikim?
 
Enough... she said do you think you can do smuggling, should
I smuggle?

163
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:47,000
Wele, qaçaxçîtiya te jî wî wextî fêde nake... tu wî wextî
nikanî...
 
Wow, your smuggling wouldn't have helped then either... you
couldn't at that time...

164
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:50,000
Pêşî me dikir, min ya Rebî aleme, 20-30 ciya me da riya...
yekî çû yekî hat...
 
We used to do it, oh Lord of the worlds, 20-30 times we set
out... one went, one came...

165
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:51,000
Wele.
 
Really.

166
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:52,000
Em rind bûn.
 
We were good.

167
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Seheta te xweş be, seheta we xweş.
 
Bless you, bless you.

168
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:56,000
Xalo me ku, li vê derê me pirs kir...
 
Uncle, when we, we asked around here...

169
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:59,000
Mêrikek me re dibê 700 mal e... yekî me jê re ji pirs kir,
dibê 300 e.
 
A man tells us it's 700 houses... we asked someone else, he
says it's 300.

170
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:05,000
Yanî yek ji wan dibêje 300, yek... 750... 300... bes me
nehesibandiye, we ededê gund?
 
So one of them says 300, one... 750... 300... but we haven't
counted, do you know the village's number?

171
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:09,000
Eses... Me qeyd li balediyê heta 270 nehatiye derketin...
 
Basically... we registered at the municipality and it hasn't
exceeded 270...

172
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:10,000
Eywa. Wekî din tu nizanî.
 
Alright. Otherwise you don't know.

173
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:12,000
Wekî din... em negeriyane.
 
Otherwise... we haven't looked into it.

174
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:15,000
Xalo, ev tebîeta wî çawa ye? Tebîeta şeran e?
 
Uncle, how is its nature? Is it a nature of fights?

175
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:16,000
Tebîeta şeran e, lê...
 
It's a nature of fights, yes...

176
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:17,000
Xelk her gav yanî ne go dinav gundan...
 
So people are always, not like in the villages...

177
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:21,000
Kehrebe wele qet dîrokê me qut kirine... Xwedê jê razî
bin...
 
They have cut our electricity in history... may God be
pleased with them...

178
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:22,000
Ewa e.
 
Yes, it is.

179
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:23,000
... qut kirin.
 
... they cut it.

180
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,000
Eywa.
 
Alright.

181
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:27,000
Têlefon ji me qut kirin, hel kirin birin...
 
They cut our phones too, they removed them and took them...

182
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:31,000
Û mêrikek hat, go têkçûyî, me... çêkirin û, got ez pêk tînim
her yek 400 dolar bidin.
 
And a man came, he said it's broken, we... fixed it, and he
said I'll set it up if each gives 400 dollars.

183
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:32,000
Mixtar filitî, go e...
 
The mukhtar escaped, he said...

184
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:33,000
Feqar in.
 
They are poor.

185
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:35,000
Go hûn tev feqar in... gund tev nabe, nabe...
 
He said you are all poor... the whole village can't do it,
can't...

186
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:37,000
Ev kes kî 400 dolar bide, ji kê bixwazim?
 
Who here can give 400 dollars, who should I ask from?

187
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Xalo te di şopê gundî da... hûn raqîb in da, we 400 dolar
nedaye...
 
Uncle, you tracked it in the village... you observed, you
didn't give 400 dollars...

188
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:44,000
Weleh, hat... mêrik sê çar caran jê hat...
 
Swear to God, he came... the man came three or four times...

189
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:46,000
Tîcaret e, tîcaret e, ew...
 
It's a business, it's a business, that...

190
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,000
Tîcareta we wilo bû?
 
That was your business?

191
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:53,000
Welehî... wisa, bes e, rê xelet kirin... go... ma makîneya
we xira ye.
 
Swear to God... like that, enough, they took the wrong
way... he said... your machine is broken.

192
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:54,000
Adî ye.
 
It's ordinary.

193
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:58,000
Wî çaxî da... meselan her yekî 50 wereqe be, çi be... 25
wereqe be, me dida...
 
At that time... for example, if each was 50 bills,
whatever... if it was 25 bills, we'd give it...

194
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:02,000
Welleh bi derdek ket... bes ev bi qut kirin xelas.
 
Swear to God, it became a problem... but they cut it and
that was it.

195
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:05,000
Xalo gundê we da jî pir xirabe hene... haş pir xirabe ne.
 
Uncle, there are a lot of ruins in your village too... the
houses are very ruined.

196
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:07,000
Ê 22 mal xirab bûn.
 
Yes, 22 houses were ruined.

197
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:08,000
22 mal.
 
22 houses.

198
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:11,000
Ji niqqa de wer hatine, wekî çi pêk xirab bûne...
 
Since then they came, how did they get ruined...

199
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:15,000
Ê bes erd hejîn bû... ê min nexwest... Xwedê giravî me bes
e, pêşiya hawşa erd hejîn bûn.
 
It was just the earthquake... I didn't want it... thank God
we are enough, the earthquake happened in front of the yard.

200
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:16,000
22 mal.
 
22 houses.

201
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:18,000
Xwedê bi hewara we de be... înşallah...
 
May God come to your aid... God willing...

202
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:20,000
Em Kurmanc, cebar in, cebar.
 
We Kurmanc (Kurds) are resilient, resilient.

203
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:21,000
Înşallah, înşallah...
 
God willing, God willing...

204
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:22,000
Xirabiyê em ê dîsa çêkin. Em ê çêkin...
 
The ruins we will rebuild. We will build...

205
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:24,000
Înşallah em ê çêkin.
 
God willing we will build.

206
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:27,000
Bes... ê xalo, ez dibê ez qaçek por bikirim.
 
But... uncle, I'm thinking of buying a bit of hair.

207
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:29,000
Mele por poran kir...
 
The Mullah made hair...

208
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:33,000
Çî bas e... ew çi sebre, Xwedê sêr neke... he... dînî we...
dest wilo daye ser we.
 
What's wrong... what patience, may God not watch... your
religion... laid a hand on you like that.

209
00:22:33,000 --> 00:22:36,000
E, dibe wa cure bi cure kiriye. Bes e.
 
Yeah, it has made it varied. Enough.

210
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:38,000
Birê qesdek bi halê xwe de daçeke.
 
Let him fix his condition a bit.

211
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:40,000
Dest, me dest çêkir.
 
Hand, we fixed the hand.

212
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:41,000
Na?
 
No?

213
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:43,000
Ê me dest çêkiriye, ê çêkir, çêkirin... wekî ê te...
 
Yes, we fixed the hand, he fixed it, they fixed it... like
yours...

214
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:45,000
Na, qedarek wekî min qirika xwe por bikirya...
 
No, if I had covered my neck with some hair...

215
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:47,000
Maşallah, Xwedê emrê we dirêj bike.
 
God bless, may God give you a long life.

216
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:48,000
Sax bî, sax bî.
 
Thank you, thank you.

217
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:50,000
Xwedê wê ji we de qebûl bike.
 
May God accept it from you.

218
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:53,000
Dinya rojî ye, rojî ye... me naha jî rojî girtiye.
 
It's a day of fasting, fasting... we are fasting now too.

219
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:56,000
Silav, silav xalo...
 
Greetings, greetings uncle...

220
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:59,000
Xalo kesî te, li derve heye?
 
Uncle, do you have anyone abroad?

221
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:07,000
Silava bişîne... keçeke bi silav... xwe bişîne... bay bay
ke...
 
Send greetings... a girl with greetings... send them... wave
bye...

222
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:09,000
Silavê te ji van re. Xalo te...
 
Your greetings to them. Uncle, you...

223
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:12,000
Yek li Rûsya ye, yek li Fransa ye.
 
One is in Russia, one is in France.

224
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:14,000
Ê tu sekine, tu sekine... navê wan çi ye?
 
You wait, you wait... what are their names?

225
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:17,000
Mihemed Berekat, Ahmed Berekat.
 
Mihemed Berekat, Ahmed Berekat.

226
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:22,000
Erê, silavê me ji wan re hene. Çavên wan maçî dikim. Keçke
xalo...
 
Yes, we send them our greetings. I kiss their eyes. Girl
uncle...

227
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:25,000
Navê bavê te ye, Mihemed Elî Berekat... Ahmed Berekat...
 
It's your father's name, Mihemed Elî Berekat... Ahmed
Berekat...

228
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:28,000
Xwedê ji te razî be... ê te, xalo?
 
God bless you... and yours, uncle?

229
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:29,000
Ê min?
 
Mine?

230
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:30,000
Kenê te ye.
 
Yours is smiling.

231
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:31,000
Amir.
 
Amir.

232
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:32,000
Amir.
 
Amir.

233
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:34,000
Amir Mihemed Xelîl Mustefa.
 
Amir Mihemed Xelîl Mustefa.

234
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:37,000
Kak Amir silavê me ji te re hene... çavê te maçî dikim.
 
Brother Amir, we send you our greetings... I kiss your eyes.

235
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:40,000
Me aha.. me aha wî dî dîkran.
 
We here.. we here remembered him.

236
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:42,000
Êdî wek qedera fêrde skile...
 
It's like the fate of this place...

237
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:44,000
Qedrê te zêde.
 
You are highly respected.

238
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:47,000
Xalo dibê kê... de fêr da min di gund de...
 
Uncle says who... here in the village...

239
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:48,000
Wele?
 
Really?

240
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:50,000
Lê.. lê... tu xwedê.
 
Yes.. yes... by God.

241
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:55,000
Wela rasta te zêde ye... lê neşiyane, wela nabe wezîfe wilo
derxe...
 
By God you're right... but they couldn't, you can't just
throw out a duty like that...

242
00:23:55,000 --> 00:24:00,000
Nabe we wezîfê re derxe. Pîr e, nabe.
 
You can't take him out of his duty. He's old, it's not
possible.

243
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:08,000
Biçî wî mafî, pir giran e, wele... tişt nebe pir xirab e,
dar nebe, nav gund e... şarih e... tişt kêm in.
 
Going for that right, it's very hard, really... if there's
nothing, it's very bad, if there are no trees, it's in the
village... a street... things are lacking.

244
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:12,000
Gund... tiştekê ku esasê Xweda ne, serast in.
 
Village... things that belong to God, they are
straightforward.

245
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:24,000
Em vê xwedan... xwedanê me hene, tu kanî... hûn xwediyê
me... em serdarê me... amade xwediyê me ne. Em Xwedanê.
 
We are from this owner... we have our owner, you can... you
are our owner... you are our leader... ready to be our
owner. We are the Owner.

246
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:26,000
Em pir kêfxweş bûn, bi we.
 
We were very happy, with you.

247
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:28,000
Wela pir kêfxweş bûn.
 
By God, very happy.

248
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:31,000
Axaftin me tune ye, nexweşî me nîne.
 
We have nothing to say, we have no illnesses.

249
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:33,000
Xwedanê me... xwedanê me hene.
 
Our owner... we have our owner.

250
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:35,000
Xwedanê me heye... em... Xwedanê me heye... xwedanê me
heye...
 
We have an owner... we... We have an owner... we have an
owner...

251
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:41,000
Diçûk pirs dikî, pirs kirin... em çi hez dikin... we çi hez
nakin...
 
The little ones ask, they asked... what we like... what you
don't like...

252
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:44,000
Go îşî we umûrê we bimeşe... em kêfê bikin, tişt ne gerin...
 
They said let your work and life go on... let's enjoy, don't
look for things...

253
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:47,000
Go orduya te, me got tişt ne gerin... ahe heye.
 
They said your army, we said don't look for things... here
it is.

254
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:48,000
Eywa.
 
Alright.

255
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:51,000
Haaa. We wekî karê çû dirê kirin re nor e.
 
Yeah. It's like the work you do over there is light.

256
00:24:51,000 --> 00:24:55,000
Nizan... mêrik nezan e... me zane... vî hesabê...
 
He doesn't know... the man is ignorant... we know... this
account...

257
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:58,000
Xwendin tune bû, filan tune bû... dû ker da cut û xakin...
 
There was no reading, nothing... two donkeys plowing...

258
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:04,000
Nanê xwe bixwîn... nanê sêlê, her û derketin. Tişt ne
germin. Bes wa ye...
 
Eat our bread... bread on the sajj, and we left. Not looking
for things. That's it...

259
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:11,000
Xalo pa hûn da jî seqafe pir bûye... hûn kî dît we makîneyê
xwendiye... min pirsî, çend zanîn...
 
Uncle, then you must have had a lot of culture too... you
saw who read the machine... I asked, how much knowledge...

260
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:14,000
Em qet nizanin... gelê dî me...
 
We don't know at all... other people...

261
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:17,000
Wey limin... dema dixwînin, kê nexwendiye ez nizanim.
 
Oh my... when they read, who hasn't read, I don't know.

262
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:20,000
Ez nizanim.. min nexwendiye...
 
I don't know.. I haven't read...

263
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:22,000
Bîrin.
 
Tell them.

264
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:26,000
Bîrin... na wele em tiştekî, bes ew e.
 
Tell them... no, by God, we nothing, that's it.

265
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:29,000
Me gel de ez re em qet sekin, naway e?
 
We were with the people, I swear we stopped entirely, isn't
it so?

266
00:25:29,000 --> 00:25:32,000
Naway e, bavê min go naway e. Na na, ez qet nizanim te.
 
No way, my father said no way. No no, I don't know you at
all.

267
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:35,000
Te dît, min mar kir.. ta de divê wî tajî...
 
You saw, I made a snake... until you have to give that
greyhound...

268
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:38,000
Na... le... duqanê nabe... xelas...
 
No... yes... there's no shop... finished...

269
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:40,000
Înşallah, înşallah xalo...
 
God willing, God willing uncle...

270
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:45,000
E çê be... xwedanê me çê bibe... serwerê me hene, mezinê me
hene, tixtorê me hene.
 
Let it be good... let our owner be good... we have our
leaders, we have our elders, we have our doctors.

271
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:46,000
Elhemdulilah..
 
Praise be to God..

272
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:49,000
Qe ortê... reîsê me çi bînî.
 
In the middle... whatever our president brings.

273
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:54,000
Wela rasta te ye.. em bîst û şeş sal in min xizmetê lê
wekir, min tixtora vir tixtora Haleb dest ser min.
 
Swear to God you're right.. I served there for twenty-six
years, I took doctors from here, doctors from Aleppo laid
hands on me.

274
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:55,000
Ev a..
 
This is it..

275
00:25:55,000 --> 00:25:59,000
Wela rasta. Înşallah tiştek wilo, hûn ji tiştek wilo pêk
bînin..
 
Swear to God you're right. God willing something like that,
you bring something like that to life..

276
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:01,000
Ji xelkê bixwazin.
 
Ask the people.

277
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:07,000
Tixtor e nexweşxane ye, nexweşxane ye weke bîkin... ko hûn
biçin doxtoran wilo me pir zehmet dît, xilas... pir milet,
pir nexweşek dîn e.
 
Doctors and hospitals, hospitals as you build them... when
you go to doctors like that we faced a lot of hardship,
enough... a lot of people, a lot of crazy sick people.

278
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:14,000
Milet pir e... meko yek ji we xwarin... min go yekî ez
xwarim. Kê nexweş e heta navê xwe fêrke tu bi min re xeber
dide?
 
There are many people... I fed one of you... I said I fed
one. Who is sick enough to learn their name while talking to
me?

279
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:17,000
Wela tu rasta xwedê tiştek we ye te piştê me de...
 
Swear to God you are right, God's thing is behind us...

280
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:21,000
Da em em de werim ku em wî destûra em wî derbas bikin... ev
wilo ye tîştek pîs bi.
 
Let's let me come so we can pass that rule... it's like
that, it became a bad thing.

281
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:26,000
E pîs e. Wela wisa bi, rasta wisa ye wela we bi...
 
It is bad. Swear to God it was like that, it's true it was
like that, swear to God...

282
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:29,000
E bîda ye. Wela... rasta...
 
Yeah it's the beginning. Swear to God... right...

283
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:33,000
Bes, înşallah... înşallah xwedanê me... ew xwedanê, ew xwedî
heq. Xwedê pêk werin.
 
But, God willing... God willing our owner... that owner,
that rightful owner. May God make it happen.

284
00:26:33,000 --> 00:26:38,000
Em înşallah em pêşkevin... em însan, Kurmanc. Em a, em qewat
in, cebbari ne.
 
We, God willing, will advance... we people, Kurmanc (Kurds).
We are, we are strong, we are resilient.

285
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:39,000
Qewat in, e!
 
Strong, yeah!

286
00:26:39,000 --> 00:26:41,000
Tev a em nexweşiya...
 
All of us illnesses...

287
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:43,000
Xwe tezkere yan em di nava...
 
Our ID or we are inside...

288
00:26:43,000 --> 00:26:49,000
Tezeker... naskirin xalo, te we naskin em serbilind in. Hûn
jî serbilind in... û înşallah nêzîk da.. tu mafê xwe
bibîne...
 
ID... knowing uncle, you know us, we are proud. You are
proud too... and God willing soon.. you will see your
right...

289
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:51,000
Înşallah. Em wî qewlê din rast bikin.
 
God willing. Let's correct that other word.

290
00:26:51,000 --> 00:26:54,000
Înşallah înşallah...
 
God willing, God willing...

291
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:58,000
Xwedê heqê... xwediyê... tiştê we bide. Milet bi xêr û
bereket in...
 
May God give the right... the owner's... your things. The
people are blessed and abundant...

292
00:26:58,000 --> 00:27:01,000
Em dixwazin wî parastin em...
 
We want to protect him we...

293
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:05,000
Em wilo din xwedê nizanin.. wele min ew ne dît...
 
We don't know the other like God.. swear to God I haven't
seen it...

294
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:11,000
Lê.. em naxwazin pir... xwe re tiştê em xwe derbas kin.. nas
kir.
 
Yes.. we don't want too much... to pass our things for
ourselves.. known.

295
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:15,000
Em wî dervî.. min ji devê... mîrî yê we bi em bî...
 
We from outside.. from my mouth... of your prince with us...

296
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:19,000
Em gî zanin xalo.. bes em dixwazin... daxwaza me dîsa te...
 
We all know uncle.. but we want... our request to you
again...

297
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:23,000
Em carek bi wî aliyê din re deng we bibin.. qene em tiştek
pêk bînin.
 
Let's raise your voice to the other side once.. maybe we can
achieve something.

298
00:27:23,000 --> 00:27:27,000
Çê bibe me nizan... qene mafê wan heye.
 
We don't know if it will happen... at least they have their
right.

299
